Unit: F-60. src/__tests__/typecheckIsNotVacuous.test.ts pinned CI to
`tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json`; CI was widened to `tsc -b
tsconfig.json` (F-52, both projects). The test was stale, not the
workflow. Reproduced on pristine 69a7f87: 1 failed | 8 passed.

Cause, not symptom: the assertion checked a spelling instead of the
property the file exists for. It now extracts the single tsc `run:`
from typecheck.yml and requires (1) build mode over the solution file,
the only form that follows references; (2) no -p/--project, so it can
never be narrowed to one project; (3) tsconfig.json still references
both tsconfig.app.json and tsconfig.node.json, so "both" stays true.

Shown failing first on three planted workflow copies — narrowed to one
project, vacuous -p on the solution file, bare tsc --noEmit — each
1 failed | 8 passed; then 9 passed on the real workflow, which was
restored byte-for-byte. The stale header sentence is corrected too
(Standing Rule 21).

Evidence: docs/evidence/d2/f60/.

